invariant: INV-51
file: Makefile
catches: test/lint-schedule-order.sh
reason: unit_cflags returns -fno-schedule-insns2 for every source, so a
  gcc build for x86-64 compiles the whole packaged object with its second
  scheduling pass off. The ruling of 2026-10-11 gives the flag to
  sha512_avx2.c alone: no other file was measured without the pass, and
  the other kernels' recorded timings are of code compiled with it. Every
  test passes. make lint-schedule-order asks make for the commands a gcc
  build for x86-64 runs and requires that the one that compiles sha512.c
  for the packaged object carries no such flag.

--- old
unit_cflags = $(if $(filter sha512_avx2.c,$(1)),$(SHA512_AVX2_GCC_CFLAGS))
--- new
unit_cflags = $(SHA512_AVX2_GCC_CFLAGS)
